# The same for a free name read as an ACTUAL: id(x) before and after poke (which writes the root's x through node) answers 10 both times: probe answers
# 10 * 1000 + 10. An ordinary row by the norm; it does NOT witness the hold -- it passes without any take in the readers (the source is a row of the caller's frame).
# наблюдение явной записью: локалы не публикуются (#flush-receiver-contract)
(
    Observed:
        int: r 0
)
int: x 10
fn: id (int: v) int
    return: v
sub: poke ()
    node\x := 99
fn: probe () int
    int: first id(x)
    poke()
    int: second id(x)
    return: first * 1000 + second
int: r probe()

sub: main ()
    @: shared node[0]
    shared\Observed\r := r
main()
